## Ce que ce papier dit sur la forme de la mémoire (pour l'axe « traces brutes ou résumé »)


Il compare les deux, pour une mémoire de l'**exécutant** tenue au fil d'un harnais qui grossit, et le sens dépend du cas :
- agent seul, axe des outils, source EOG : les formes résumées font mieux que la mémoire brute (38,6 et 36,9 contre 33,0 ; p. 8, p. 28) ;
- agent seul, axe des compétences, source EOG : la mémoire brute fait autant ou mieux (21,6 ± 1,0 contre 20,9 ± 2,0 et 19,6 ± 0,6 ; tableau 4, p. 8) ;
- systèmes à plusieurs agents : les auteurs concluent que les trajectoires concrètes réussies sont le choix le plus sûr (p. 30).

## Quickstart  {% id="quickstart" %}


Requires SDK 3.2 or later (`pip install -U google-genai` or
`npm install @google/genai@latest`). Pass a model, shared input, and a map of
questions. Each question requires a type ([`noul`](/docs/decisions-api#noul) for
yes/no) and instructions:

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input="The blue mug I ordered on Monday arrived cracked on Wednesday.",
      questions={
          "is_damaged": {
              "type": "noul",
              "instructions": "Did the item arrive damaged?",
          },
      },
  )

  answer = result.answers["is_damaged"]
  print(f"P(yes)={answer.noul:.2f} confidence={answer.confidence:.2f}")
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.mjs" label="JavaScript" %}
  ```javascript
  import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

  const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiVersion: "v1beta" });

  const result = await ai.decisions.create({
    model: "gemini-decision-1",
    input: "The blue mug I ordered on Monday arrived cracked on Wednesday.",
    questions: {
      is_damaged: {
        type: "noul",
        instructions: "Did the item arrive damaged?",
      },
    },
  });

  const answer = result.answers?.is_damaged;
  if (answer?.type === "noul") {
    console.log(`P(yes)=${answer.noul} confidence=${answer.confidence}`);
  }
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.sh" label="REST" %}
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/decisions" \
    -H "x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "gemini-decision-1",
      "input": "The blue mug I ordered on Monday arrived cracked on Wednesday.",
      "questions": {
        "is_damaged": {
          "type": "noul",
          "instructions": "Did the item arrive damaged?"
        }
      }
    }'
  ```

  {% /tab %}

{% /tabs %}

The API returns calibrated probabilities and token usage:

```json
{
  "answers": {
    "is_damaged": { "type": "noul", "noul": 0.99, "confidence": 0.99 }
  },
  "usage": {
    "total_input_tokens": 100,
    "input_tokens_by_modality": [{ "modality": "text", "tokens": 100 }],
    "total_output_tokens": 0,
    "total_tokens": 100
  }
}
```

## Question types  {% id="question-types" %}


### Yes or no (noul)  {% id="noul" %}

A yes/no question returns the calibrated probability that the answer is yes. Add
criteria to define what yes and no mean when the question alone is ambiguous.

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input="Customer returned the sweater because they preferred green over blue.",
      questions={
          "is_defect": {
              "type": "noul",
              "instructions": "Is the customer reporting a product defect?",
              "criteria": {
                  "true_description": "The product itself is broken or faulty.",
                  "false_description": "Preference, sizing, shipping, or pricing complaint.",
              },
          },
      },
  )

  print(result.answers["is_defect"].noul)
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.mjs" label="JavaScript" %}
  ```javascript
  import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

  const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiVersion: "v1beta" });

  const result = await ai.decisions.create({
    model: "gemini-decision-1",
    input: "Customer returned the sweater because they preferred green over blue.",
    questions: {
      is_defect: {
        type: "noul",
        instructions: "Is the customer reporting a product defect?",
        criteria: {
          true_description: "The product itself is broken or faulty.",
          false_description: "Preference, sizing, shipping, or pricing complaint.",
        },
      },
    },
  });

  const answer = result.answers?.is_defect;
  if (answer?.type === "noul") console.log(answer.noul);
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.sh" label="REST" %}
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/decisions" \
    -H "x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "gemini-decision-1",
      "input": "Customer returned the sweater because they preferred green over blue.",
      "questions": {
        "is_defect": {
          "type": "noul",
          "instructions": "Is the customer reporting a product defect?",
          "criteria": {
            "true_description": "The product itself is broken or faulty.",
            "false_description": "Preference, sizing, shipping, or pricing complaint."
          }
        }
      }
    }'
  ```

  {% /tab %}

{% /tabs %}

Answer:

```json
{ "type": "noul", "noul": 0.03, "confidence": 0.97 }
```

{% callout type="note" %}
  Yes/no probabilities always fall between 0.01 and 0.99. Set thresholds inside
  that range, since a check above 0.99 never matches.

{% /callout %}

### Pick one option (choice)  {% id="choice" %}

A choice question scores a fixed set of options and returns both the top option
and the calibrated probability of every option (summing to 1). Criteria maps
each option ID to a description of when it applies. Use an empty string (`""`)
when the option ID is self-explanatory.

Before evaluation, the API sorts option keys alphabetically in UTF-8 byte
order. Changing key order in your JSON request doesn't change option positions,
and exact probability ties break to the alphabetically first key.

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input="I was charged twice for my order.",
      questions={
          "department": {
              "type": "choice",
              "instructions": "Which department should handle this request?",
              "criteria": {
                  "billing": "Payments, invoices, and refunds.",
                  "technical": "Problems using the product.",
                  "shipping": "Delivery and tracking.",
                  "other": "Anything outside these categories.",
              },
          },
      },
  )

  answer = result.answers["department"]
  print(answer.choice, answer.confidence, answer.probabilities)
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.mjs" label="JavaScript" %}
  ```javascript
  import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

  const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiVersion: "v1beta" });

  const result = await ai.decisions.create({
    model: "gemini-decision-1",
    input: "I was charged twice for my order.",
    questions: {
      department: {
        type: "choice",
        instructions: "Which department should handle this request?",
        criteria: {
          billing: "Payments, invoices, and refunds.",
          technical: "Problems using the product.",
          shipping: "Delivery and tracking.",
          other: "Anything outside these categories.",
        },
      },
    },
  });

  const answer = result.answers?.department;
  if (answer?.type === "choice") {
    console.log(answer.choice, answer.confidence, answer.probabilities);
  }
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.sh" label="REST" %}
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/decisions" \
    -H "x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "gemini-decision-1",
      "input": "I was charged twice for my order.",
      "questions": {
        "department": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Which department should handle this request?",
          "criteria": {
            "billing": "Payments, invoices, and refunds.",
            "technical": "Problems using the product.",
            "shipping": "Delivery and tracking.",
            "other": "Anything outside these categories."
          }
        }
      }
    }'
  ```

  {% /tab %}

{% /tabs %}

Answer:

```json
{
  "type": "choice",
  "choice": "billing",
  "probabilities": { "billing": 0.99, "shipping": 0.004, "other": 0.003, "technical": 0.002 },
  "confidence": 0.99
}
```

{% callout type="note" %}
  Choice questions always distribute probability across your options, even when
  none fits. Threshold confidence to catch low-certainty inputs, pair the
  question with a separate yes/no scope check, or add a catch-all option such as
  "other" with an explicit description. Avoid positional keys like
  "none_of_the_above": alphabetical sorting places it ahead of keys like
  "shipping" and "technical" instead of last.

{% /callout %}

### Rate on a scale (score)  {% id="score" %}

A score question rates the input across ordered levels. Criteria is an array of
non-empty level descriptions ordered from lowest to highest (2 to 255 levels,
with 2 to 10 recommended for most rubrics), indexed starting at 0.

The returned score is the probability-weighted average of the level indices, so
it can fall between levels, and legend maps each index back to its description.

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input="Export fails in Safari but works in Chrome.",
      questions={
          "severity": {
              "type": "score",
              "instructions": "How severe is this issue for the user?",
              "criteria": [
                  "Cosmetic: appearance only, no lost functionality.",
                  "Workaround available: a task fails, but another way works.",
                  "Fully blocked: a task fails with no workaround.",
              ],
          },
      },
  )

  answer = result.answers["severity"]
  print(answer.score, answer.confidence, answer.probabilities)
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.mjs" label="JavaScript" %}
  ```javascript
  import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

  const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiVersion: "v1beta" });

  const result = await ai.decisions.create({
    model: "gemini-decision-1",
    input: "Export fails in Safari but works in Chrome.",
    questions: {
      severity: {
        type: "score",
        instructions: "How severe is this issue for the user?",
        criteria: [
          "Cosmetic: appearance only, no lost functionality.",
          "Workaround available: a task fails, but another way works.",
          "Fully blocked: a task fails with no workaround.",
        ],
      },
    },
  });

  const answer = result.answers?.severity;
  if (answer?.type === "score") {
    console.log(answer.score, answer.confidence, answer.probabilities);
  }
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.sh" label="REST" %}
  ```bash
  curl -X POST "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/decisions" \
    -H "x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "model": "gemini-decision-1",
      "input": "Export fails in Safari but works in Chrome.",
      "questions": {
        "severity": {
          "type": "score",
          "instructions": "How severe is this issue for the user?",
          "criteria": [
            "Cosmetic: appearance only, no lost functionality.",
            "Workaround available: a task fails, but another way works.",
            "Fully blocked: a task fails with no workaround."
          ]
        }
      }
    }'
  ```

  {% /tab %}

{% /tabs %}

Answer:

```json
{
  "type": "score",
  "score": 1.12,
  "legend": {
    "0": "Cosmetic: appearance only, no lost functionality.",
    "1": "Workaround available: a task fails, but another way works.",
    "2": "Fully blocked: a task fails with no workaround."
  },
  "probabilities": { "0": 0.03, "1": 0.83, "2": 0.15 },
  "confidence": 0.83
}
```

Because different probability distributions can produce the same expected
value (here 1.12, sitting just above level 1), check the per-level
probabilities and confidence alongside the score when inputs can split across
levels.

Use the score to rank inputs or filter candidate results against a rubric
threshold. When your code needs a discrete level, pick the entry with the
highest probability:

```python
level = max(answer.probabilities, key=answer.probabilities.get)  # "1"
print(answer.legend[level])  # "Workaround available: ..."
```

To compare scales with different numbers of levels, divide the score by the
highest level index to normalize it between 0 and 1.

## Ask multiple questions  {% id="multiple-questions" %}


Put independent questions about the same input in one request. Shared input
counts once per request regardless of how many questions you ask (each question
adds only its own instructions and criteria), and question types can be mixed.
This example routes a support ticket using order data and the customer message.

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  import json
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  order = {"order": {"id": "8821", "item": "headphones", "price_usd": 240}, "tier": "Gold"}
  message = {"message": "Audio cuts out on the left earcup. Fix it today or I cancel my membership."}

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input=[
          {"type": "text", "text": json.dumps(order) + "\n"},
          {"type": "text", "text": json.dumps(message)},
      ],
      questions={
          "is_defect": {
              "type": "noul",
              "instructions": "Does `message` describe a hardware defect?",
          },
          "next_action": {
              "type": "choice",
              "instructions": "What is the right resolution given `tier` and `order`?",
              "criteria": {
                  "instant_refund": "Refund without return. Low value or clear fault.",
                  "replacement_shipment": "Ship a replacement. Customer returns the original.",
                  "troubleshooting_flow": "The issue may be fixable by the customer.",
                  "human_escalation": "",
              },
          },
          "churn_risk": {
              "type": "score",
              "instructions": "How likely is the customer to churn if the issue is not resolved now?",
              "criteria": [
                  "No churn signal",
                  "Mild frustration",
                  "Mentions alternatives",
                  "Threatens to cancel",
              ],
          },
      },
  )

  a = result.answers
  if a["is_defect"].noul > 0.9 and a["next_action"].confidence > 0.6:
      action = a["next_action"].choice
  else:
      action = "human_escalation"

  print(action, a["churn_risk"].score)
  ```

  {% /tab %}

  {% tab filename="decisions.mjs" label="JavaScript" %}
  ```javascript
  import { GoogleGenAI } from "@google/genai";

  const ai = new GoogleGenAI({ apiVersion: "v1beta" });

  const order = { order: { id: "8821", item: "headphones", price_usd: 240 }, tier: "Gold" };
  const message = { message: "Audio cuts out on the left earcup. Fix it today or I cancel my membership." };

  const result = await ai.decisions.create({
    model: "gemini-decision-1",
    input: [
      { type: "text", text: JSON.stringify(order) + "\n" },
      { type: "text", text: JSON.stringify(message) },
    ],
    questions: {
      is_defect: {
        type: "noul",
        instructions: "Does `message` describe a hardware defect?",
      },
      next_action: {
        type: "choice",
        instructions: "What is the right resolution given `tier` and `order`?",
        criteria: {
          instant_refund: "Refund without return. Low value or clear fault.",
          replacement_shipment: "Ship a replacement. Customer returns the original.",
          troubleshooting_flow: "The issue may be fixable by the customer.",
          human_escalation: "",
        },
      },
      churn_risk: {
        type: "score",
        instructions: "How likely is the customer to churn if the issue is not resolved now?",
        criteria: ["No churn signal", "Mild frustration", "Mentions alternatives", "Threatens to cancel"],
      },
    },
  });

  const { is_defect, next_action, churn_risk } = result.answers ?? {};
  let action = "human_escalation";
  if (
    is_defect?.type === "noul" && next_action?.type === "choice" &&
    (is_defect.noul ?? 0) > 0.9 && (next_action.confidence ?? 0) > 0.6
  ) {
    action = next_action.choice ?? action;
  }
  console.log(action, churn_risk?.type === "score" ? churn_risk.score : undefined);
  ```

