## Input  {% id="input" %}


The input field accepts text, image, audio, video, and PDF document blocks
using the same content block schema as the
[Interactions API](/docs/interactions-overview) (tool-call, tool-result, and
thought blocks aren't supported):

```none
Input   = string | Content | Content[]
Content = TextContent | ImageContent | AudioContent | VideoContent | DocumentContent
```

| Block | Fields | Supported MIME types |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `text` | `text` | n/a |
| `image` | `data` or `uri`, `mime_type`, optional `resolution` | `image/png`, `image/jpeg`, `image/webp`, `image/heic`, `image/heif`, `image/gif`, `image/bmp`, `image/tiff` |
| `audio` | `data` or `uri`, `mime_type` | `audio/wav`, `audio/mp3`, `audio/mpeg`, `audio/aiff`, `audio/aac`, `audio/ogg`, `audio/flac`, `audio/m4a`, `audio/opus`, `audio/webm`, `audio/l16`, `audio/alaw`, `audio/mulaw` |
| `video` | `data` or `uri`, `mime_type`, optional `resolution` | `video/mp4`, `video/mpeg`, `video/mov`, `video/avi`, `video/webm`, `video/wmv`, `video/x-flv`, `video/3gpp` |
| `document` | `data` or `uri`, `mime_type` | `application/pdf` |

*   Inline data accepts base64-encoded bytes (up to 100 MB per request, or
    50 MB for PDFs).
*   URI inputs accept [Files API](/docs/files) URIs (`file.uri`) and public or
    signed HTTPS URLs (up to 15 MB per external URL).
*   Always set the MIME type to the real file format. The API rejects generic
    octet-stream types and content that doesn't match the block type.
*   The API concatenates adjacent text blocks in `input` and `instructions` in
    order with no separator. Include your own spaces or newlines (`\n`) between
    blocks.
*   Input can't be empty.

### Structured data  {% id="structured-data" %}

Serialize JSON objects and arrays to a string and pass them as text so keys
inside your payload stay plain data rather than content blocks. In your
question instructions, refer to JSON fields by their key path:

```python
state = json.dumps({"customer": {"tier": "Gold"}, "order": {"id": "8821", "age_days": 14}})
```

### Documents (PDF)  {% id="documents" %}

Pass a PDF up to 50 MB as inline base64 bytes. For larger or reusable files,
upload them with the [Files API](/docs/files). The model reads text, tables,
charts, and page layouts together. This example checks an invoice PDF for a
purchase order number and routes it to an expense category:

{% tabs %}
  {% tab filename="decisions.py" label="Python" %}
  ```python
  import base64
  from google import genai

  client = genai.Client(http_options={"api_version": "v1beta"})

  with open("invoice.pdf", "rb") as f:
      pdf_b64 = base64.b64encode(f.read()).decode("utf-8")

  result = client.decisions.create(
      model="gemini-decision-1",
      input=[
          {
              "type": "document",
              "data": pdf_b64,
              "mime_type": "application/pdf",
          },
      ],
      questions={
          "has_po_number": {
              "type": "noul",
              "instructions": "Does the invoice include a purchase order (PO) number?",
          },
          "expense_category": {
              "type": "choice",
              "instructions": "Which expense category fits this invoice?",
              "criteria": {
                  "cloud_infrastructure": "Servers, GPU compute, hosting, or storage.",
                  "software_licenses": "SaaS subscriptions or seat licenses.",
                  "travel": "Flights, hotels, meals, or ground transport.",
                  "other": "Anything outside these categories.",
              },
          },
      },
  )

  po = result.answers["has_po_number"]
  category = result.answers["expense_category"]
  print(po.noul, category.choice, category.confidence)
  ```

  {% /tab %}

